page('about.html','About',head('Our story','Rooted in Odisha.<br>Open to the world.','A monthly meeting place for poems in Odia, Hindi and English.')+'<img class="about-art" src="assets/odisha-watercolour.webp" alt="Soft watercolor study of wetland plants, water and an Odisha-inspired shoreline."><div class="side-layout"><div class="prose"><span class="eyebrow">Proposed editorial introduction</span><p>Some words carry the fragrance of the place they come from. Others open a door to somewhere we have never been. This journal makes room for both.</p><h2>A familiar name. A fresh page.</h2><p>Kabita Live continues with the name its readers know. Its renewed visual identity gives that familiar literary home a more expressive Odia presence.</p><p class="or" lang="or">ମାଟିର ମହକ · ମନର ସ୍ୱର</p><p>The fragrance of earth. The voice of the heart.</p><h2>A familiar poetic invitation.</h2><p><em>“Poetry is an echo, asking a shadow to dance.”</em></p><p>The existing epigraph stays with the journal, welcoming readers across its three languages.</p></div><aside class="side-panel"><span class="eyebrow">The editorial desk</span><h2>Pradeep Biswal</h2><p>Editor</p><h2 style="margin-top:28px">Paresh Kumar Pattnaik</h2><p>Managing Editor</p><a class="text-link" href="contact.html">Write to the editors ↗</a><hr style="border:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin:25px 0"><h2>Your words belong here.</h2><p>Visit the submissions page for the path from a manuscript to the journal.</p><a class="text-link" href="submit.html">Sending a poem ↗</a></aside></div>','About','Mission, identity refresh, both signatures and editorial team.')
page('submit.html','Submissions',head('For poets','Send us your words.','Poetry in Odia, Hindi and English. A simple, human route to the editorial desk.')+'<div class="side-layout"><div>'+''.join(f'<section class="step"><span class="eyebrow">0{i}</span><div><h2>{title}</h2><p>{body}</p></div></section>' for i,title,body in [(1,'Keep the poem’s shape.','Include the poem title, your preferred name and the original line and stanza breaks.'),(2,'Tell us about the work.','Identify its language and let the editor know if it is a translation or has appeared elsewhere.'),(3,'Introduce yourself.','Add a short biography and the contact address you would like the editors to use.')])+'<div class="notice">These are proposed submission prompts. File formats, eligibility, permissions, deadlines and response expectations must be confirmed by the editor before launch.</div></div><aside class="side-panel"><h2>By email</h2><p>Use the journal’s existing editorial address.</p><p style="overflow-wrap:anywhere;margin:20px 0">kabitaliveweb@gmail.com</p>'+btn('Open email draft','mailto:kabitaliveweb@gmail.com?subject=Poetry%20submission')+'<p class="small muted" style="margin-top:20px">Your email app opens a draft. Nothing is sent automatically.</p></aside></div>',desc='Clear submission preparation and existing email route; no invented deadline.')
